 its performance advantages in inference speedups.\n*   **Date:** The date "MARCH 18, 2024" is displayed in the top-right corner, indicating when the information was last updated or presented.\n\n**Visual Representation:**\n\nThe flowchart is presented on a black background, with green and purple accents used to highlight key components and steps. The use of simple icons and clear labels makes the flowchart easy to follow and understand. Overall, the image effectively communicates the capabilities and architecture of NeMo Retriever,', 'similarity score': 0.592085599899292}, {'4996': '4996', 'text': 'frames/frame_5001 seconds: The image presents a flowchart illustrating the process of NeMo Retriever, a system designed to facilitate the retrieval and analysis of data from various sources. The flowchart is divided into several sections, each representing a different stage in the process.\n\n*   **NeMo Retriever**\n    *   The flowchart begins with the "NeMo Retriever" section, which is highlighted in green.\n    *   This section includes two sub-components: "Vector Database" and "RAPIDS cuVS Accelerated Indexing" and "RAPIDS cuVS Accelerated NN Search".\n    *   The "Vector Database" is further broken down into three sub-components: "Embedding Microservices", "Retrieval Microservices", and "Text-to-SQL Microservice".\n    *   These sub-components are represented by orange cylinders with green logos, indicating the different types of data being processed.\n    *   The "Embedding Microservices" component is connected to the "Plan" section, suggesting that the output of this stage is used to inform the planning process.\n*   **Chat with PDF**\n    *   The flowchart also includes a section titled "Chat with PDF", which is highlighted in green.\n    *   This section appears to be a user interface for interacting with the NeMo Retriever system.\n    *   It features a chat window with a graph and text, as well as a button labeled "NVIDIA L4 Tensor Core GPU vaults ahead".\n   